{
  "format": "optibench-workstation",
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "appVersion": "0.1.0-alpha",
    "author": "Optibench examples",
    "created": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "description": "Unregulated linear PSU. A 230 V rms / 50 Hz mains source (325 V peak) feeds a 20:1 step-down transformer (~16 V peak on the secondary). A bridge rectifier of four diodes (D1..D4) conducts in pairs on alternate half cycles, a 1000 uF reservoir capacitor smooths the output to about 14 V DC with a few hundred mV of 100 Hz ripple, feeding a 470 ohm load and a green power LED with a 1 k resistor. Probe SEC shows the secondary waveform, probe OUT the smoothed DC (watch it charge up over the first cycles).",
    "dimension": "2d",
    "modified": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "title": "Transformer Power Supply"
  },
